# Maintainer: Yūrei Linux project
# Yūrei's own recipe (stage 3, the desktop; docs/INDEPENDENT.md). The source
# address and sum are the ones in independent/bootstrap/sources.lock;
# check-recipes.py keeps them the same.
pkgname=libdrm
pkgver=2.4.124
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Userspace interface to the kernel's graphics drivers (DRM)"
arch=(x86_64)
url="https://dri.freedesktop.org/"
license=(MIT)
depends=(glibc systemd)
source=("https://dri.freedesktop.org/libdrm/libdrm-$pkgver.tar.xz")
sha256sums=('PIN')

build() {
    # no libdrm_intel: it needs libpciaccess, and Mesa's Intel drivers
    # don't use it
    meson setup libdrm-$pkgver build --prefix=/usr --buildtype=release \
        -D udev=true -D intel=disabled -D valgrind=disabled -D tests=false \
        -D man-pages=disabled -D cairo-tests=disabled
    ninja -C build
}

package() {
    DESTDIR="$pkgdir" ninja -C build install
}
